        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs excerpt on parsed arguments. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A failed parse, an invalid context count, or no target is returned as a failure. A target that gives no lines prints its state in its own text, so one bad target does not hide the others.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>arguments</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The parsed arguments from getArguments. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>input</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The supplied input text, or nullopt for the process standard input. It holds one target per line when the arguments name none.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The exit code, the output documents, and the failures. The exit code is 0 when every target gives lines, 1 when one does not, and 2 on a failure. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
